# Teaching and Learning about Genocide: Questions of Content, Rationale, and Methodology.

**Authors:** Parsons, William S., Totten, Samuel

## Abstract
Points out there has been an increase in curricular materials for the study of genocide. Maintains that teachers need a rationale for teaching about genocide to help them select appropriate content. Provides examples of rationales from leading educators and delineates three teaching models. Includes curricular resources and an eight-item bibliography. (SLM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ427719

